Wed Jan  7 15:21:12 2026 Alan Dayton
v1.55.6
Reviewers: Peter Robinson, Ben Liu

Checks for approve tag during the verifyCompletedReview step of publish.

* Checks that the tag exists

* Checks that it contains the required information

* Checks that it is on the same commit as the source branch or that the diffs with respect to develop are unchanged

For what a review rule looks like in the .grapeconfig, see https://rzlc.llnl.gov/gitlab/GRP/test_application_1/-/merge_requests/5/diffs. That merge request also shows what the merge request description will contain for the approval. Here's what the corresponding tag looks like:

'''

git show dc_4

tag dc_4

Tagger: Alan Dayton <dayton8@llnl.gov>

Date:   Tue Jan 6 15:52:56 2026 -0800

Derivative Classifier Review(s)

Derivative Classifer: dayton8

Guide(s): fdsfs

Reason: None

commit 32ed8d73e80e17c9b15c205b908c1ecc288441e8 (tag: dc_4)

Author: Alan Dayton <dayton8@llnl.gov>

Date:   Tue Jan 6 11:15:30 2026 -0800

    Add new file

diff --git a/new_change.txt b/new_change.txt

new file mode 100644

index 0000000..8b13789

--- /dev/null

+++ b/new_change.txt

@@ -0,0 +1 @@

+

'''

